<p>The kind of car you drive plays a major role in your insurance rates. Certain vehicles are more likely to be stolen or vandalized. For example, older cars may have weaker security systems, making them easier targets for theft. Luxury cars, on the other hand, are coveted by thieves, meaning they can cost more to insure.</p>
